The Öhri family cooks dinner in the evening and then watches a film together: {{1}}
The bakery in Triesen bakes bread and sells it in the shop: {{2}}
The Landtag passes a new law to protect young people: {{3}}
Mr Matt works as a baker in the morning, baking Zopf bread in the bakery: {{4}}
In the evening, Mr Matt shops for his family at the supermarket: {{5}}
The municipality has the road in front of the school building resurfaced with tarmac: {{6}}
A schoolgirl earns her first wages in a holiday job: {{7}}
A furniture shop pays its employees their monthly wages: {{8}}
Ms Banzer teaches at the state school – the national authorities pay her wages from tax revenue: {{9}}
After school, Ms Banzer pays for her shopping at the checkout: {{10}}
